#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""extorq-collect-dispatch: the only program the extorq-collector SSH key can run.

Installed root:root 0755 as /usr/local/sbin/extorq-collect-dispatch. sshd forces
it for the collector account twice: ``Match User extorq-collector`` ->
``ForceCommand`` and the key's ``restrict,command=`` options. It parses
``$SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND`` strictly and runs a fixed allow-list of read-only
collection commands as the unprivileged collector user (groups adm and
systemd-journal; no sudo). No shell is ever invoked, no caller-supplied path is
ever opened, every subprocess has a fixed argument vector, a timeout and a
bounded output, and every response is size-limited.

Grammar (tokens separated by exactly one space, printable ASCII only):
    version
    journal <cursor|-> <max_entries 1..5000>
    audit <inode|-> <offset> <max_bytes 4096..1048576>
    inventory
    packages
    posture
Anything else: "denied" on stderr, exit status 77. Protocol version 1; output
formats are documented in docs/telemetry/linux.md.

Python 3 standard library only (Ubuntu 24.04 ships Python 3.12).
"""

